/-
# The degree-23 modular equation (for Entry 3.29)

`χ(q)χ(q²³) − χ(−q)χ(−q²³) = 2q + 2q³/(χ(−q²)χ(−q⁴⁶))` (`M23`): the degree-23 equation of Schröter and Ramanujan
(Berndt, *Ramanujan's Notebooks III*, p. 551, Entry 15(i)) in the form used by Yesilyurt (JMAA 388 (2012), (4.28)).

After multiplying by `f(−q)f(−q²³)` it is `φ(−q²)φ(−q⁴⁶) − 2q³ψ(−q)ψ(−q²³) − φ(−q)φ(−q²³) = 2q f(−q)f(−q²³)`
(`P23`). This is the determinant-23 analogue of Cao's (71) (Entry 3.18, `E18.lean`): in `ℂ((t))` with `t² = q`,
`A − B = t²C` for the three forms of determinant 23
* `A = Σ (−1)^{x+y} t^{4x²+2xy+6y²}` (`LA23`: `φ(−q²)φ(−q⁴⁶) − 2q³ψ(−q)ψ(−q²³)`),
* `B = Σ (−1)^{x} t^{2x²+2xy+12y²}` (`LB23`: `φ(−q)φ(−q²³)`),
* `C = Σ (−1)^{x} t^{3x²+2xy+8y²+x+8y}` (`LC23`: `2f(−q)f(−q²³)`),
glued by the index-2 covers `(1 1; −1 1)` of `A` and `(2 0; 0 1)` of `B` and `C` (`S23a`, `S23b`, `S23c`) and three
unimodular changes of variables (`S23r`, `S23s`, `S23t`). The forms and maps were found by
`scripts/forty/round8/m23a.py`, `m23b.py`, `m23c.py`; the Lean is generated by `gen_e29a.py`.
-/
